## 0. How to Use This PRD With Spec Kit

This document is written so an agent can turn it directly into Spec Kit artifacts. It deliberately separates **what/why** (feature intent, user value, acceptance criteria — belongs in `spec.md`) from **how** (stack, architecture, file layout — belongs in `plan.md`), per Spec Kit's own guidance not to mix the two at the specify stage. Section 7 ("Technical Reality & Constraints") is the one exception: it's collected in one place *specifically* so it can seed `/speckit.constitution` and inform `/speckit.plan`, rather than being scattered across feature descriptions.

Suggested workflow:

1. **Place this file at the repo root** as `PRD.md` (or per-repo if frontend/backend are separate repos — see §7.1).
2. **Run `/speckit.constitution` once**, pointing the agent at §7 (Technical Reality & Constraints) and §8 (Global Non-Functional Requirements). These become the project's standing rules that every later spec, plan, and task is checked against.
3. **Run `/speckit.specify` once per Epic** (§11.1–§11.6), not once for the whole PRD — each epic is already scoped to one sprint and one feature branch, which is exactly Spec Kit's grain. Feed the agent the specific epic section plus §9 (Data Entities) and §13 (Traceability Matrix row) for that epic. Suggested feature directory naming: `specs/001-foundation-auth/`, `specs/002-health-profile/`, `specs/003-food-meal-tracking/`, `specs/004-dashboard-reporting/`, `specs/005-ai-insights/`, `specs/006-admin-testing-deployment/` — matching Sprints 1–6.
4. For **Epics 1–2 (already implemented)**, use `/speckit.specify` to *reverse-document* the existing Next.js + Laravel implementation into `spec.md`, rather than to plan new work — the "Current Implementation Notes" callouts in §11.1–§11.2 exist for this purpose. This gives the rest of the project a real spec to diff against instead of a gap.
5. Run `/speckit.clarify` before `/speckit.plan` on any epic with an item listed under "Open Questions" in §15 — those are exactly the ambiguities Spec Kit's clarify step is meant to surface and resolve.
6. Run `/speckit.plan`, `/speckit.tasks`, and `/speckit.implement` per epic as normal. Because the backend is a separately-owned Laravel service that is already built and tested (see §7.2), plans for Sprints 3–6 should treat "extend the Laravel API" and "extend the Next.js frontend" as two coordinated but separately-planned tracks within the same feature, not a single full-stack scaffold.
7. Keep this PRD as the versioned source; when a story's acceptance criteria change, edit this file first and re-run the affected `/speckit.specify` → `/speckit.plan` → `/speckit.tasks` chain, per Spec Kit's "spec is the authority, re-derive" model.

