## 7. Technical Reality & Constraints

> **This section supersedes SRS §1.8–§1.9 for anything already built.** The original SRS specified a React web app + Flutter mobile app on Laravel SQL Server. The team pivoted for the actual build. Feed *this* section, not the SRS's tech chapter, into `/speckit.constitution` and `/speckit.plan`.

### 7.1 Actual stack in use

| Layer | Planned in SRS | **Actually built** |
|---|---|---|
| Web frontend | React 19 | **Next.js (App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4)** — `healthylife-ai-web` repo |
| Mobile frontend | Flutter 3.x | Not yet started — still open for Sprint-by-sprint planning; revisit stack choice before Sprint 3 |
| Backend | Laravel API (13) | **Laravel**, deployed at `https://backend-repository-production.up.railway.app/api`, tested via Postman |
| Database | SQL Server | Managed by the Laravel backend team; not directly owned by the frontend track |
| Auth | JWT (as specified) | **Confirmed: JWT.** Access token returned as `authorization.access_token` in the response body, sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Refresh token is a rotating, one-time-use, HttpOnly cookie (`POST /auth/refresh`). Account locks for 15 minutes after 5 failed login attempts (429 response) — matches SRS NFR-02. |
| Localization | react-i18next or similar | Custom lightweight `LocaleProvider` (ar/en dictionaries, RTL via `<html dir>`), synced server-side via `PATCH /user/locale` |
| Interface design | Stitch prototyping tool | Stitch design system already produced and implemented ("Calm Data" style: color tokens, spacing, radii — already ported into Tailwind config) |

**Implication for `/speckit.plan`:** the backend is a separate, already-implemented, already-tested service. Plans for Sprints 3–6 should not scaffold backend infrastructure from scratch — they should (a) confirm/extend the Laravel API contract with the backend team, then (b) plan the Next.js integration against that contract, treating the Laravel API as an external dependency with its own release cadence.

### 7.2 Confirmed backend API surface (Sprints 1–2, from the team's Postman collection)

| Endpoint | Method | Auth | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `/auth/register` | POST | — | `full_name, email, password, password_confirmation, preferred_language?`. Auto-logs in on success. |
| `/auth/login` | POST | — | `email, password`. 429 after 5 failed attempts (15 min lock). |
| `/auth/logout` | POST | Bearer | Revokes refresh token, invalidates JWT. |
| `/auth/refresh` | POST | Cookie (`refresh_token`) | Rotates refresh token, issues new access token. Detects token-theft replay. |
| `/user/locale` | PATCH | Bearer | `preferred_language: ar\|en`. |
| `/profile` | POST | Bearer | Health profile create/update. Accepts **metric** (`height_cm`, `weight_kg`) or **imperial** (`height_ft`+`height_in`, `weight_lb`) units. |
| `/weight-logs/{id}` | PUT | Bearer | `weight_kg, recorded_date`. **Confirmed.** |
| `/weight-logs` | POST, GET | Bearer | **Unconfirmed** — left as empty placeholders in the Postman collection. Frontend currently assumes standard Laravel REST conventions (create/list). **Must be confirmed with the backend team before Sprint 3 planning locks this in** (see §15, Open Questions). |
| *(none yet)* `/nutrition/daily-needs` or similar | — | — | **Does not exist yet.** US-03 (daily calorie/macro calculation) is currently computed **client-side** in the Next.js app (Mifflin-St Jeor formula) as a stand-in. This is a real gap to close — see §15. |

### 7.3 Known integration gaps vs. this PRD's scope

- **FR-01d (password reset)** is in the SRS and in the User Story catalog's US-01, but is **not yet implemented** in the current frontend (Sprint 1 shipped register/login/logout only) and does not appear in the Postman collection. Needs its own spec pass before it can be considered part of "Sprint 1, done."
- **Weight-log create/list routes** are unconfirmed (§7.2). Frontend behavior here is a best-effort assumption, not a verified contract.
- **Daily nutrition calculation** (FR-03/US-03) has no backend endpoint yet; frontend computes it locally as a fallback.
- **Mobile (Flutter) app**: not started. FR-10 (cross-platform sync) and NFR-08 (compatibility) currently apply to the web app only.

