### 11.1 Epic 1 — Foundation & Authentication (Sprint 1) — **Status: Implemented**

**Sprint goal:** set up the project repository, environment, and localization framework; deliver secure authentication so users can register, log in, and log out in Arabic or English.

**Definition of Done:** repo/CI/coding standards in place · registration, login, logout work end-to-end and pass QA on web (and mobile, when built) · Arabic/English localization verified on all Sprint 1 screens.

**Current implementation notes:** live in the Next.js app at `/`, `/register`, `/login`; wired to `POST /auth/register`, `POST /auth/login`, `POST /auth/logout`, `POST /auth/refresh`. Language toggle syncs to `PATCH /user/locale`. **Password reset (FR-01d) is not implemented** — treat as a follow-up spec, not covered by the acceptance criteria below.

#### US-01a — User Registration
*Related FR: FR-01a · Story Points: 5 · Dependencies: none*

> As a new user, I want to create an account using my email and password, so that I can securely access the HealthyLife AI platform.

| AC | Given | When | Then |
|---|---|---|---|
| AC-1 | A visitor is on the registration screen | They submit a unique email + a password meeting minimum strength rules | The system creates the account and logs them in automatically |
| AC-2 | A visitor submits registration | The email is already registered | The system rejects it and displays an error, prompting a different email |
| AC-3 | A visitor submits registration | The password is weak | The system displays password strength requirements before allowing submission |

#### US-01b — User Login & Localization
*Related FR: FR-01b, FR-01c, FR-09 · Story Points: 5 · Dependencies: US-01a*

> As a registered user, I want to log in with my credentials and choose my preferred language (Arabic or English), so that I can access my account and use the platform in the language I understand best.

| AC | Given | When | Then |
|---|---|---|---|
| AC-1 | A registered user is on the login screen | They submit valid email + password | The system authenticates via JWT and grants access to the dashboard |
| AC-2 | A registered user submits login | Credentials are invalid | The system shows a generic error without revealing which field was wrong |
| AC-3 | Any user | They toggle the language switch | The interface reloads in the selected language and text direction (RTL/LTR) |
| AC-4 | A user has 5 consecutive failed login attempts | The 5th failure occurs | The account locks for 15 minutes (HTTP 429) |

**Use Case UC-01 (Register / Login / Reset Password)** — Primary actor: New/Registered User. Precondition: none (register) or account exists (login/reset). Postcondition: user holds a valid authenticated session, or password is reset.
- *Main flow:* open auth screen → choose register/login/reset → enter details → submit → system validates → system creates account / authenticates / updates password → issues session token, shows dashboard (or confirms reset).
- *Alternative — duplicate email at registration:* system detects duplicate → shows notice → redirects to login/recovery.
- *Exception — auth failure:* invalid credentials/validation error → nothing is created/started/reset → clear error shown, retry allowed → after 5 consecutive failed logins, 15-minute lock.

**Data entities:** `User`, `UserToken`.

